VENDORED INTO THE TREE — no manifest, therefore invisible to license_finder
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added 2026-08-28 (UNI.3, inbound-obligation pass). These were absent from this
file for a structural reason worth recording, because it will recur: the
inventory above is assembled from MANIFESTS (license_finder for gems, npm/forge
for contracts, conda/pip-licenses for tools), and our per-file gate
(scripts/spdx_headers.rb) deliberately DENY-lists `vendor/` — correctly, since we
must not stamp OUR SPDX onto someone else's file. Both decisions are right on
their own; together they left the one surface we actually REDISTRIBUTE as bytes
with no instrument looking at it. There is no root package.json at all, and
Leaflet arrives as a bare `pin "leaflet"` line in config/importmap.rb, so no
manifest names it anywhere.

  - Leaflet 1.9.4 ............ BSD-2-Clause
      (c) 2010-2023 Vladimir Agafonkin, (c) 2010-2011 CloudMade
      Files: vendor/javascript/leaflet.js
             vendor/assets/stylesheets/leaflet/leaflet.css
             vendor/assets/stylesheets/leaflet/images/*.png  (5 sprites)
      Notice: vendor/javascript/LICENSE-leaflet.txt  (ONE home; the stylesheet
             directory carries a pointer, not a copy). The bundle keeps its own
             `@preserve` banner, but the CSS and the sprites carried no notice at
             all — and BSD-2-Clause requires it to travel with the redistribution.
  - JetBrains Mono (variable subsets) ... SIL OFL 1.1
      Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors; repackaged by Fontsource
      Files: vendor/assets/fonts/jetbrains-mono/*.woff2  (latin, latin-ext, cyrillic)
      Notice: vendor/assets/fonts/jetbrains-mono/LICENSE (full OFL text, already
             adjacent — the obligation to carry the text was met; only the
             inventory entry was missing)

